# sys-elevator: Veilstone Department Store. From 1F into the elevator,
# ask the receptionist for 4F (menu entry 1): the script sets the special location (4F warp 2, decomp
# SetSpecialLocation) and plays the elevator ride; the exit mat (a dynamic warp) lands on 4F. The
# `elevator-door` (the BTP0 door opening) and `elevator-ride` (the lights) screenshot lines are the
# browser spec's key beats.
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_VEILSTONE_STORE_1F 15 3 up
until idle
+0 press up
+6 screenshot elevator-door
until state player.zone "platinum:MAP_HEADER_VEILSTONE_STORE_ELEVATOR"
+0 release up
until idle
# from the mat (3, 6) one step west to (2, 6), then face the receptionist at (1, 6)
+0 press left
until position 2 6
+0 release left
until idle
+0 press left
+1 release left
until idle
+0 assert facing player left
+0 press a
+1 release a
# the greeting has two pages, then the floor menu
advance text
# the menu takes input after its 3-tick delay
+3 press down
+1 release down
+1 press a
+1 release a
# "Certainly." waits for A; the ride starts after it
until message
+0 press a
+1 release a
+44 screenshot elevator-ride
advance text
until idle
+0 assert state specialLocation {"zone": "platinum:MAP_HEADER_VEILSTONE_STORE_4F", "warp": 2, "x": 18, "z": 2, "facing": "down"}
# back onto the exit mat (3, 6), a WARP_ENTRANCE_SOUTH tile: pushing down on it warps
+0 press right
until position 3 6
+0 release right
until idle
+0 press down
until state player.zone "platinum:MAP_HEADER_VEILSTONE_STORE_4F"
+0 release down
until idle
+0 assert map platinum:MAP_HEADER_VEILSTONE_STORE_4F
